※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4525

※ A default belongs to every call of the function, including calls in files
※ this one has never seen, and a caller there has none of the names this
※ definition could use.  So what is written has to be a value the compiler
※ settles here, once, and hands over unchanged at every call.  C++ takes the
※ other road -- the expression is looked up in the definition's scope and
※ worked out afresh at each call -- which needs a scope to travel with the
※ function, and nothing here carries one.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = plus(1u8)
    0u6

fn plus(n: u8, by: u8 ← n) → u8:
    n + by
